  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Isotorachrysone may be associated with the Raji cell line through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Isotorachrysone to Ataxin-2, which is then targeted by a complex involving Oleamide, ultimately leading to the Raji cell line. The second pathway connects Isotorachrysone to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is also targeted by the same complex, again leading to Raji. These findings indicate that Isotorachrysone may act as a modulator of a complex that targets Raji cells through different molecular mechanisms. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a potential role for Isotorachrysone in influencing Raji cell behavior via the regulation of Ataxin-2 and the proteasome complex. The strength of the evidence is supported by the high final scores in all three paths, but the exact mechanism by which Isotorachrysone influences Raji cells remains to be fully elucidated."
